{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1557876-honed-senses-gift-plus-other-perception-related-gifts","id":1557876,"title":"Honed Senses Gift plus other perception-related Gifts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-01-24T10:59:50-08:00","id":1557876,"title":"Honed Senses Gift plus other perception-related Gifts","content":"What do you think, dear forumites? Honed Senses gives you an exceptional success on 3 successes instead of 5 for perception rolls. The most straightforward reading would be that this applies only to the basic Wits + Composure perception roll, but what about something like Scent the Unnatural, which is very much a kind of perception roll, or Prey on Weakness, things like that? What about tracking rolls? Uses a different system, but I'm thinking more of the concept here. How would y'all do it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-24T11:26:17-08:00","id":1557879,"title":"","content":"It uses Perception with a capital P, which is a system term denoting the basic Wits + Composure roll, and in flavor is sharpening your wolf senses. I wouldn't apply it to any gift activation roll, nor would I directly apply the exceptional success effect to other rolls. I do think it could be a good basis for circumstantial dice bonuses on some rolls, like tracking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0